  "description": "Takanini covers some of Auckland’s southernmost suburbs, including Conifer Grove, Randwick Park, and Totara Heights. The electorate is held by National’s Rima Nakhle, who first won election in 2023 with a margin of 21,936. National also won a majority of the party vote with 53%, followed by Labour with 28%. The electorate is in one of New Zealand’s fastest growing areas population-wise: it was first created as an entirely new electorate in 2020, and was 17.7% over population quota in the 2026 redistributions. \n\n\n",
